WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:02.260
- Good evening, everyone.

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.880
And welcome to the
Academy of Motion Picture

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.840
Arts and Sciences Governors Awards.

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.800
Now there's nothing that can take away

00:00:10.989 --> 00:00:12.140
from the splashiness

00:00:12.140 --> 00:00:16.310
and the enormous significance
of Sunday's 94th Oscars.

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:18.990
But for those of us who've been fortunate

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:20.040
to attend this event,

00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:23.720
it's perhaps even closer to our hearts.

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:27.580
It's more intimate, it's
private, not televised.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:29.780
It involves a cocktail
hour and a free meal.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:35.250
And, most important, it
represents a generosity of spirit

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.793
that's not always in
the Hollywood spotlight.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:42.110
This night exists because the
Academy's Board of Governors

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:43.920
has taken a moment to step back

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:47.370
from the focus on this
year's singular achievements,

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:50.623
which are astounding and many,

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:54.923
to honor four individuals
we love and adore.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:58.560
Not only for their
specific accomplishments,

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.770
but for their creative careers

00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:03.690
and influential lives well lived.

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:08.690
These four gorgeous humans
have each gone above and beyond

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:12.663
having a unique and an
indelible mark to leave.

00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.490
And we are all the lucky
beneficiaries of their talent,

00:01:16.490 --> 00:01:19.270
their insight, and their legacy.

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:21.880
Over the years, we've come to trust them

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:25.350
for their integrity and
their creative bravery.

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:28.520
We've been eager to hear
more and more from them.

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.510
And we're grateful for the love affair

00:01:31.510 --> 00:01:32.960
that we, and audiences everywhere,

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.963
have had with each of them for years.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:38.940
Now here's a little inside baseball story.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.280
Each year, the Academy's governors

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.660
gather for a board meeting

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:46.030
where they suggest recipients
for an honorary award.

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:46.863
It's normally a meeting

00:01:46.863 --> 00:01:49.950
full of lengthy speeches
and presentations,

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:52.010
analysis and debate,

00:01:52.010 --> 00:01:53.480
and multiple rounds of voting,

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.780
which go on for hours and hours,

00:01:56.780 --> 00:01:58.720
ending with a picked over fruit platter

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:01.140
and a lot of doodling on legal pads.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:04.430
But this year, lightning quick.

00:02:04.430 --> 00:02:07.700
Fervent advocacy, giddy enthusiasm,

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.550
and rapid-fire consensus.

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.779
Sam Jackson, hell yeah.

00:02:11.779 --> 00:02:14.779
(audience cheering)

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.219
Elaine May, genius.

00:02:20.219 --> 00:02:21.869
(audience cheering)
Yes, please!

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:28.419
Liv Ullmann, a goddess
of acting and directing.

00:02:28.419 --> 00:02:30.643
(audience cheering)
Bam!

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:38.070
And humanitarian Danny Glover, God bless.

00:02:38.070 --> 00:02:41.273
Done!
(audience cheering)

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.680
If only all our board
meetings were that brief

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:48.463
and that harmonious.

00:02:49.510 --> 00:02:51.430
So we can thank those
extraordinary men and women,

00:02:51.430 --> 00:02:54.210
representing the Academy's 17 branches,

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:56.810
for their year-round, tireless work

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.660
and their great taste in honorees.

00:02:58.660 --> 00:03:01.811
Will our esteemed governors please rise?

00:03:01.811 --> 00:03:04.811
(audience clapping)

00:03:18.390 --> 00:03:21.100
Okay, board meeting adjourned.
(audience laughing)

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.080
I'd also like to take
a moment to thank Rolex

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:25.410
for its generous support of this evening,

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.690
and of the Academy, and
the museum year round.

00:03:28.690 --> 00:03:29.540
Thank you, Rolex.

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:36.260
And now, here's a line I
couldn't ever say often enough,

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:38.175
ladies and gentlemen, Bill Murray.

00:03:38.175 --> 00:03:41.175
(audience clapping)

